      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-18T12:15:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Daniel, \n\nA gentle reminder to review the comments and respond.\n\nThanks,",
      "revId": "e72f5746a422d8d8625b089ba58cd777081509e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "644c4a28_6f339dd4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-18T22:30:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could this be accomplished by passing the physical address to GuestAddress offset as a parameter to the load_elf function instead? For aarch64, we would pass `AARCH64_PHYS_MEM_START` and for x86, we would just pass 0. Then the load address could be calculated as `GuestAddress(phdr.p_paddr + phys_to_guest_offset)` and nothing else would need to change (hopefully).\n\nI am not really comfortable with the tricky behavior change based on special fields in the first program header.",
      "revId": "e72f5746a422d8d8625b089ba58cd777081509e9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
